The  driver  provides  the  capability  of  combining one or more
disks/partitions into one virtual disk.   This  document  assumes
that  you’re  familiar with how to generate kernels, how to prop‐
erly configure disks and pseudo‐devices in a kernel configuration
file, and how to partition disks.  Note that  the  partitions  of
the disks be combined.  Each component partition should be offset
at  least  one cylinder from the beginning of the component disk.
This avoids potential  conflicts  between  the  component  disk’s
disklabel  and  the disklabel.  The kernel will only allow compo‐
nent partitions of type But for now, it allows partition  of  all
types  since some port lacks support of an on‐disk BSD disklabel.
